BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T000000
UID:260606XlXHNXT6Ck2Y3rh8mQIv3Q
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market is a year-rou
 nd Saturday tradition in Sonoma County\, bringing together local farmers\,
  ranchers\, food artisans\, and neighbors from 8:30 a.m. to 1 p.m. This is
  not just a place to shop\, it's a place to connect directly with the peop
 le who grow your food. As a Slow Food Sonoma County award recipient\, the 
 market prioritizes integrity\, seasonality\, and true farm-to-community re
 lationships. Expect peak-season produce harvested just hours before market
 \, pasture-raised meats\, fresh flowers\, artisan breads\, handcrafted goo
 ds\, and thoughtfully prepared foods that reflect the region's agricultura
 l richness. Visitors can stroll the vibrant open-air market\, sample local
  flavors\, and experience Sonoma County's food culture in its most authent
 ic form. Families\, chefs\, and weekend explorers alike gather here to dis
 cover what's growing now and to support small farms that keep our local fo
 od system strong. Open every Saturday\, rain or shine\, the Santa Rosa Ori
 ginal Certified Farmers Market is a cornerstone of the community and a mus
 t-visit stop for anyone wanting to taste\, shop\, and experience Sonoma Co
 unty at its freshest.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T170000
UID:2604304RPb3i21L0uDeRCf4CA2tQ
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Lavender Workshop | Make + Take
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T150000
UID:261120qZSQ3xiRwEetG6H8JsY2Pg
DESCRIPTION:Lavender Workshop: Create\, Relax &amp\; Enjoy\n\nSpend a rela
 xing afternoon immersed in the soothing scent of lavender! In this hands-o
 n workshop\, you'll create your own lavender products to enjoy at home or 
 share as thoughtful gifts.\n\nEach participant will make and take home two
  lavender sprays and two lavender sugar scrubs. All materials are provided
 \, so just bring your creativity and get ready for a fun\, fragrant aftern
 oon! Additional sprays and scrubs will also be available for purchase.\n\n
 Additional sprays and scrubs will also be available for purchase.\n\nAll m
 aterials included.\n\nAbout MaryEllen: \n\nMaryEllen Whitton is an award-w
 inning author\, speaker\, personal growth coach\, and workshop facilitator
  guiding others to create what comes next with greater clarity\, confidenc
 e\, and intention.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center - Gallery (standing room)
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/the-art-of-lavender-worksh
 op-make-take?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Opening at Reichwage Winery: Paintings and Artisan Wood Creati
 ons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T160000
UID:261112-VU5WGrtxk66YexxXBHs4g
DESCRIPTION:**Join us for an afternoon celebrating art\, nature\, and crea
 tivity with local artists Jann Aanestad and Ken Hower. Meet the artists\, 
 explore their work\, and enjoy light bites in the lovely setting of Reichw
 age Winery. Wine by the glass and tastings will also be available for purc
 hase.**\n\n***Resilience | Jann Aanestad***\n\nJann's colorful paintings c
 apture the beauty of nature\, the stories held in familiar places\, and qu
 iet moments in everyday life. Inspired by her own remarkable journey of re
 covery and renewal\, her work celebrates resilience\, the transformative p
 ower of light\, and the beauty that surrounds us.\n\n***Shaped by Nature |
  Ken Hower***\n\nKen creates beautiful artisan woodwork\, transforming wal
 nut\, oak\, manzanita\, and olive into one-of-a-kind bowls\, platters\, bo
 ards\, and decorative art. His pieces celebrate the natural grain\, rich t
 extures\, and flowing organic shapes of wood\, highlighting the unique cha
 racter and beauty of each piece.\n\nCome for the art\, stay for the atmosp
 here\, and discover the hidden gem that is Reichwage Winery.
LOCATION:Reichwage Winery
URL:https://www.reichwage.com/upcoming-events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Redwood Chorale's 20th Anniversary!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T150000
