BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Grateful Gathering: A Thanksgiving Celebration of The Grateful
  Dead
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T203000
UID:261111tqzQlRv6O0ubIDIo6-eSEQ
DESCRIPTION:Happy Deadsgiving!\n\nMarcus Rezak is a nationally touring gui
 tarist and bandleader known for his explosive improvisation and genre-bend
 ing style. Leader of the Grateful Dead project Shred Is Dead\, Rezak has 
 collaborated with members of Umphrey’s McGee\, Trey Anastasio Band\, Fra
 nk Zappa’s band\, Blues Traveler\, Little Feat\, and more. A Berklee and
  DePaul graduate\, he brings a deep love of improvisational music and a fe
 arless\, high-energy approach to every performance.\n\nJoin us for a festi
 ve celebration of the music of The Grateful Dead\, Jerry Garcia and beyond
 . \n\nThis event is a fundraiser for the Sebastopol Center for the Arts.\
 n\nWith\n\nAnna Elva \\(Stu Allen\\)\n\nSteve Pile \\(Terrapin\, Phil Lesh
 \\)\n\nStephanie Salva \\(Stu Allen\, Tumbleweed Soul\\)\n\nSteven Younger
  \\(Alamo Mission\, Zigaboo Modeliste\\)\n\nSam Betty \\(Flowstone\, The M
 ight as Well Band\\)\n\nMatt Petruska \\(Flowstone\, The Might as Well Ban
 d\\)
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://engage.sebarts.org/event/the-grateful-gathering/e828904
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
