UID:260929rJH5gt5zx0qKrzPMvqrXGA
DESCRIPTION:THURSDAY NIGHTS WITH DJ BRXNDO OPEN FORMAT • REQUESTS • DA
 NCING • NO COVER\n\nThursday nights have a new home in The Lounge at Bar
 rel Proof. Every Thursday at 9 PM\, DJ BRXNDO takes over the front room wi
 th an open-format set built around the crowd\, the dance floor and your re
 quests.\n\nBRXNDO has been making his way through the Bay Area nightlife s
 cene\, spinning parties from Santa Rosa to San Francisco. Now he's settlin
 g into a weekly Thursday night residency at Barrel Proof.\n\nOpen format m
 eans just that: no single genre gets to run the night. BRXNDO can move thr
 ough Reggaeton\, Hip-Hop\, Latin hits\, Top 40\, throwbacks\, dance tracks
  and party favorites depending on where the room takes him.\n\nHear someth
 ing you want? Make a request.\n\nSome Thursdays might lean Latin. Some mig
 ht turn into a throwback party. Some nights might go somewhere completely 
 different. BRXNDO reads the room and keeps it moving.\n\nWhatever else is 
 happening at Barrel Proof that night\, The Lounge belongs to BRXNDO every 
 Thursday at 9.\n\nDJ BRXNDO Every Thursday 9 PM The Lounge at Barrel Proof
  501 Mendocino Ave • Downtown Santa Rosa 21+ No Cover\n\nCheck out **www
 .BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/thursday-nights-with-dj-brxndo-live-in-th
 e-lounge-tickets-2002239002756?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T170000
UID:260914ooi1IqfkhkeL6Bk-wtX_5A
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present *“Antarctica: The 
 Frozen Desert\,”* a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\,
  opening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November. 
  The exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after
  more than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity
 \, he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar reg
 ions. The exhibit features work generated over 6 *voyages to the* Antarcti
 c Peninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Fal
 klands and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photogra
 ph.\n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on
  Earth\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely
  outside of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of 
 years ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 year
 s. Defined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — 
 vast\, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a 
 kind of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever be
 fore.
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T193000
UID:26041571F4AYGtJUClWR2uJB3glg
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! **
 Samba no Pé** (Samba in the Foot) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\n**You will learn**\n\nThe Basic S
 tep: You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Sa
 mba no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic 
 flair\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n
 \nTechnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to h
 elp you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: Y
 ou will learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible be
 at of the bateria (the samba drum section).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway #8 San Rafael\
 , CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowe
 d.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8 • San Rafael\, CA 94903
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
