BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 ACORN MUSH BLUES FESTIVAL
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T210000
UID:261120QlJ8ea-4sk-iCg0bK6XILw
DESCRIPTION:American blues and roots music is treasured by all\, and certa
 inly in the Native American community as well. The Acorn Mush Blues Festiv
 al highlights local native musicians and artists who over the years crafte
 d their own style of that music. Just as acorns are gathered and processed
  into a fine delicious meal\, so is the music. Weaving Blues\, country\, r
 ock\, pop\, Jazz\, and R&B with our traditional native music.\n\nPomo Cult
 ural series - Presented by the Lake County Arts Council
LOCATION:Soper Reese Theatre
URL:http://soperreesetheatre.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Very Merry Weekend
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T180000
UID:261116vu9qgHSQDkOFiYkA3fU7Lg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for A Very Merry Weekend at Montgomery Village!\n\nCel
 ebrate the season with a weekend of exclusive retail offerings\, family-fr
 iendly entertainment\, festive trimmings at every turn\, and more.\n\nFrid
 ay\, November 27:\n\nLive holiday music from 12pm-2pm in The Courtyard\, c
 ourtesy of Jimmy Galvan.\n\nHoliday caroling from 3:30pm to 5:30pm across 
 property\, courtesy of Silver Belles Caroling Group.\n\nSaturday\, Novembe
 r 28:\n\nWeekend Santa Sightings begin! Photos with Santa take place in Th
 e Courtyard on weekends from Saturday\, November 28 to Sunday\, December 2
 0\, 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. daily. Appointments are highly recommended. A portio
 n of proceeds from Weekend Santa Sightings benefit Sonoma County Secret Sa
 nta Program. Book your spot here.\n\nCelebrate Small Business Saturday by 
 supporting local small businesses across the Village.\n\nCelebrate the sea
 son at our Second Annual Tree Lighting Celebration on Saturday\, November 
 28\, from 5–7 p.m. in The Courtyard!\n\nEnjoy a festive evening filled w
 ith holiday music\, creative activities\, and a special appearance by Sant
 a and Mrs. Claus. Admission is free\, with seasonal fun for the whole fami
 ly:\n\nLive holiday music and carolers\, plus a family-friendly holiday si
 ngalong at 6:45 p.m.\n\n\\- Complimentary hot cocoa\n\n\\- Churros and coo
 kies available for purchase\n\n\\- Complimentary caricature portraits\n\n\
 \- Custom wood-burned gift tags\n\n\\- Make-your-own mini snowmen and jing
 le bell wreath ornaments\n\n\\- Write your letters to Santa\, delivered th
 rough the official Montgomery Village Santa Mail mailbox\n\n\\- A special 
 visit from Santa and Mrs. Claus\n\n\\- Make the evening a little sweeter w
 ith a stop at Salt & Straw. During the event\, enjoy a complimentary scoop
  with the purchase of a scoop\, available November 28\, 2026\, from 5–7 
 p.m.\n\nSunday\, November 29:\n\nLive holiday music in The Courtyard\n\nAB
 OUT SONOMA COUNTY SECRET SANTA\n\nSonoma County’s Secret Santa is a nonp
 rofit gift-giving program\, providing gifts and holiday cheer to those les
 s fortunate in our community.\n\nSecret Santa has been bringing joy to peo
 ple throughout Sonoma County for over 30 years\, ensuring that children\, 
 teens\, adults\, and seniors who would not otherwise receive a holiday gif
 t have reason to celebrate and experience the compassion and generosity of
  their community.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village - Courtyard
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/a-very-merry-weekend-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zumba with Janeth
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T121500
UID:261116h6BVKoK-n0axCtu9MCbBBQ
DESCRIPTION:Turn up the music\, torch calories\, and start your weekend wi
 th pure energy!\n\nJoin Janeth every Friday from 11:00 AM to 12:15 PM at S
 alsa Dance Marin for an exhilarating 75-minute dance fitness party. Whethe
 r you want to tone up\, boost your stamina\, or simply let loose on the da
 nce floor\, this class blends high-energy.\n\nWhat to Expect in zumba with
  Janeth:\n\n• Full-Body Warm-Up: Awaken your muscles\, activate your cor
 e\, and elevate your heart rate safely.\n\n• The Dance Party Workout: Hi
 gh-energy choreography set to salsa\, cumbia\, merengue\, reggaeton\, and 
 pop beats. Fast and slow rhythms alternate for interval training that maxi
 mizes calorie burn.\n\n• Cool-Down & Lengthening Stretch: Dedicated stre
 tching to restore flexibility\, release muscle tension\, and leave you fee
 ling refreshed and empowered.\n\nClass Details:\n\n• When: Fridays | 11:
 00 AM – 12:15 PM \\(75 Minutes\\)\n\n• Where: Salsa Dance Marin \, 414
 0 Redwood hwy 8\, san Rafael\n\n• Instructor: Janeth\n\n• Level: All f
 itness levels welcome — modifications available for beginners and high-i
 mpact dancers alike. No prior dance experience needed!\n\n• What to Brin
 g: Comfortable workout attire\, supportive athletic shoes\, a water bottle
 \, and a sweat towel.\n\nCome for the workout\, stay for the party — res
 erve your spot on the dance floor this Friday!
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/zumba-with-janeth/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Hike at Sugarloaf
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T120000
UID:261116APOjfNfrm0WKT8joxri3Iw
DESCRIPTION:Join our Docents on this fun family hike that is good for all 
 ages\, where you will learn about Sugarloaf Park\, its plants\, animals\, 
 and history. \n\nThe hike begins from the Visitor Center. One option head
 s down to the waterfall on the 2-mile Pony Gate-Canyon loop\, while a seco
 nd\, shorter option will meander along the Creekside Nature Trail. Please 
 note the route is bound to change depending on logistics such as wet cross
 ings and the participants' physical ability. Free event\, RSVP required. W
 ear layers\, appropriate footwear for slippery/rocky trails\, bring at lea
 st 32oz of water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a snack. Parking fees
  apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026greenfriday
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
