BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DJ Cal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T220000
UID:261109HvyU7UdaDU22JxpJ2AzLJw
DESCRIPTION:Raised in the Bay Area\, DJ Cal has gained a reputation for do
 ing multi-genre set lists designed to move the crowds with a blend of Trap
 \, EDM\,Hip-Hop and Reggaeton music. He calls the city of Santa Rosa his h
 ome\, but you might’ve heard his mixes on-air across the nation \\(San F
 rancisco\, Las Vegas\, Orlando\, Palms Springs\, etc.\\). He currently hol
 ds a spot as a Mixshow DJ on Fresno California B95\, with Teezzy Radio\, L
 ast Call and Friday night street party. DJ CAL has several Bay Area and No
 rthern California venues under his belt and you can catch him performing a
 nd hanging out with the hottest names in music around the Bay. He also has
  created his own day party\, "Brunch Behavior" that has gained much popula
 rity in the North Bay. Also\, his work has been supported and featured by 
 various blogs\, websites and record pools\; DJ City\, MyMP3Pool\, BpmSupre
 me and SmashTheClub\, and more. DJ CAL has worked hard to make his own mar
 k in the music industry.
LOCATION:Perch + Plow
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109110473?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T220000
UID:261108lxEDq5Ig5USyIR3MedUYtg
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\nTrigger warnings: Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in Yid
 dish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holiday Maker's Mart at Dutton-Goldfield Winery
