BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Patron Saints of Influence Fall Reading + Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T180000
UID:261031FISm3ZC9Z0yOBZhsYt2HDg
DESCRIPTION:The next Patron Saints literary reading & open mic will pay ho
 mage to mother of science fiction Mary Shelley with featured readings by L
 auren C. Johnson\, Shawna Swetech\, and Wendy M. Thompson.\n\nAs always\, 
 you are welcome to share your own written work in 5 minutes or less during
  the open mic. All words are welcome as long as they're not hateful or AI-
 generated.\n\nAbout the featured readers:\n\nLauren C. Johnson attributes 
 her upbringing in Florida–America’s weirdest state–to her interest i
 n the ecological and surreal. She's the interviews editor for The Racket J
 ournal\, where she champions experimental literature\, and is a co-founder
  and editor of Club Chicxulub\, a speculative fiction journal and reading 
 series that amplifies emerging authors. She also co-hosts Babylon Salon\, 
 one of the longest-running reading series in the Bay Area. Her short stori
 es\, interviews\, and essays have appeared in numerous journals\, includin
 g The Rumpus and Orion Magazine online. The West Façade is her debut nove
 l. Find out more at www.laurencjohnson.com.\n\nShawna L. Swetech is a ret
 ired hospital nurse\, poet\, artist and integrative health practitioner. H
 er poetry appears in Rattle\, The Healing Muse\, Pulse\, the American Jour
 nal of Nursing and other journals and anthologies. Her work ranges from th
 e personal to the universal\, the body to the body politic\, drawing from 
 the deep wells of human nature and the natural world. Shawna is a co-host 
 for the monthly reading series\, Rivertown Poets. She is the author of a n
 ewly-released poetry collection based on her 35 year career as a registere
 d nurse\, entitled “Standing in Their Fire.” \\(Kelsay Books\, 2026\\)
  www.ShawnaSwetech.com\n\nWendy M. Thompson is a poet\, writer\, and scho
 lar who hails from Oakland\, California. Her debut poetry collection Black
  California Gold \\(Bucknell University Press\, 2025\\) maps out life in t
 he Bay Area during the 1980s and 1990s and was a finalist for the 2025 Mar
 tin Cruz Smith Award: Emerging Diverse Voices prize. She has a forthcoming
  book\, Chasing the Sun: Staging Black Life\, Belonging\, and Displacement
  in California’s Bay Area \\(University of Washington Press\, 2027\\)\, 
 that looks at the cultural and performative worlds of black migrants and t
 heir descendants who staged mobility\, home\, and refusal during Second Gr
 eat Migration into the contemporary era. She is an Associate Professor of 
 African American Studies at San José State University.
LOCATION:Shady Oak Barrel House
URL:http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Women of Jack London's Beauty Ranch: Hands That Shaped the Vis
 ion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T120000
UID:261028TdpMqPiJbUuN_rkgzQVA3g
DESCRIPTION:In honor of Charmian London’s birthday on November 27\, join
  a walk celebrating her legacy and recognizing the many women whose lives\
 , work\, and creativity have helped shape the history\, culture\, and land
 scape of the park.\n\nIn the five short years Jack London lived at Beauty 
 Ranch\, he imagined it on a grand scale. That vision took root and endured
  through the labor\, intelligence\, and perseverance of two key women\, Ch
 armian Kittredge London and Eliza Shepard — who stewarded the dream\, la
 nd\, and legacy through upheaval and change\, long after Jack London was g
 one. This two-hour tour of Beauty Ranch and the House of Happy Walls Museu
 m invites visitors to step into their stories and discover how a vision be
 came an enduring reality.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-women-of-beauty-ranch-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
