BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reimagining the Rain in Corona/Capri Creek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T193000
UID:26111640OB2st-EEGikiB3c0pieg
DESCRIPTION:*Si hablas español\, habrá un intérprete en este evento. In
 dícanoslo en el último paso al inscribirte en el evento.*\n\n***What wou
 ld it look like if our neighborhoods were designed to work with and welcom
 e water instead of sending it away?***\n\nAs a part of our **Harvest the R
 ain Pilot Program**\, Daily Acts is inviting Petaluma community members wh
 o live near or are frequent visitors in the **Corona/Capri Creek** area 
 to **REIMAGINE THE RAIN** by attending an interactive\, neighborhood-based
  community input session.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**Join this Community Input Session to:**\n\n*\\-Help 
 us understand your experience with stormwater*\n\n*\\-Learn from local exp
 erts in our community*\n\n*\\-Connect with your neighbors over* ***FREE di
 nner***\n\n*\\-Provide feedback on DIY rain garden and curb cut templates*
 \n\n*\\-Enter a* ***gift card drawing*** *for local businesses like Petal
 uma Coffee & Tea\, Refill Mercantile and The Seed Bank!*\n\nDuring the ses
 sion\, we'll discuss **how we can** **work with rainwater** to build resil
 ient neighborhoods. We’ll hear from you to learn where you’ve noticed 
 water pooling in your neighborhood\, and explore whether those places are 
 creating challenges\, or if they could be the beginning of an opportunity 
 to work with water in an exciting new way! We will also gather your feedba
 ck on the rain garden and curb-cut landscape templates we’re developing.
 \n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n***lf
  you live near or frequent Corona/Capri Creek\, we want to hear from you!
 ***\n\nCome share your observations\, what you’d like to see in your nei
 ghborhood\, and any questions\, excitement or concerns you may have about 
 this pilot program. We hope to see you there!\n\n*Questions? Please email
 * ***moreinfo@dailyacts.org*** *or call* ***(707) 200-8364***
LOCATION:Petaluma Community Center (Lucchesi)
URL:https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/coronacapricreek/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T220000
UID:261108QvZAAMbeRkiaXjP0Zo8Q1w
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\nTrigger warnings: Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in Yid
 dish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Erin Durant
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T180000
UID:2610318skvuq4Gqke9W_KlCm3JxQ
DESCRIPTION:Rarely does an artist appear\, as if out of thin air\, with a 
 full body of work where lyrically lush songs carry you into other worlds a
 s if they were your own. Erin Durant's second album\, Islands is an odysse
 y of sorts\, with songs that blur the line between reality and fiction. Pr
 oduced by Kyp Malone of TV On The Radio\, the eight songs deliver clarity 
 within mystery and adventure in their uncluttered vignettes.  \n\nBorn and
  raised in New Orleans\, Durant has been based in New York for over a deca
 de\, all the while keeping track of the intricacies of life surrounding he
 r and diligently developing her craft as a songwriter and performer. Lyric
 ally\, she composes most songs on piano\, songs that tend to unfold struct
 urally like a memory or a scene from a movie. As a performer\, Durant usua
 lly transports a 232-pound ¾ size piano to venues without one. To hear he
 r play the instrument makes plain her case for the extra effort. Her music
  is rooted in an ongoing dialogue between the physicality of her playing a
 nd the high\, clear tone of her voice. Enmeshed with one another\, it’s 
 a display of an artist in full possession of herself and vision.\n\nIsland
 s sprawls out in front of you\, weaving disparate stories into an overarch
 ing narrative. The songs touch on the ability to find meaning in minutiae.
  On “Take A Load Off” Durant tells a story of a weary traveler disorie
 nted but pulled into revelry in an attempt to assuage their loss. The titu
 lar track “Islands” takes a similar tact\, focusing on the conflicting
  process of attempting to find joy when joy seems lost. Islands is a conti
 nuously shifting landscape\, with a knowing nod to the inevitability of th
 ese shifts.\n\nIslands is preceded by Durant's 2016 self-recorded album Bl
 ueberry Mountain released on New York label Flying Moonlight. Recording to
  tape in her apartment\, the lo-fi quality and stripped-down arrangements 
 led Durant to better understand the core layers of her music and from ther
 e where she wanted to go.\n\nDurant’s collaboration with Malone introduc
 ed an expansiveness in sound. She knew she wanted the songs to be fuller. 
 They welcomed instrumentation into the fold\, including a complete rhythm 
 section\, the hum of pedal steel\, and warm flourishes of brass and woodwi
 nds. These are generous songs intended to breathe. They never fall into a 
 grid. Instead\, they pause and gallop\, expand and contract\, and pass thr
 ough time unhurried.\n\n"Quietly epic songs about heartbreak\, determinati
 on\, and loneliness." - Pitchfork\n\n \n\n"There’s a movie of a whole li
 fe in her few words\, running backwards." - Greil Marcus for Rolling Stone
 \n\n \n\n"Throughout the album\, Durant’s voice shines—it’s pure and
  unwavering." - Bandcamp\n\n \n\n"Erin Durant has the same flair for couch
 ing desolate emotions in jaunty sweetness as Jenny Lewis\, Joanna Newsom a
 nd even For the Roses-era Joni Mitchell." - The Guardian\n\n \n\n"There is
  something striking about an artist who sings so wholly of a world that yo
 u find yourself transported there\, caught in the intricacies of each note
 \, each colour conjured\, each tale told\; Durant’s voice is full of wei
 ght\, a gentle sentimentality that carries you forward and return to you t
 he places she sings of\, places you don’t yet know and perhaps never wil
 l\, but ache nostalgically for."  - Gold Flake Paint\n\n \n\n"Don’t be m
 isled by Erin Durant’s lilting vocals or her sweet\, Carole King-styled 
 acoustic piano accompaniment\; that gentle exterior hides a biting\, even 
 edgy lyricist with plenty on her mind." - American Songwriter
LOCATION:Little Saint
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040654392?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
