BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paul Steward (Matinée)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T160000
UID:261115VnNbx_sp_0-ny6mNQ_kRPQ
DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n\nDoors at 4:00pm. \n\nShow from 4:45-7
 :00pm with one intermission\n\nPaul Steward is an award-winning singer and
  guitarist hailing from the San Francisco Bay Area. For over two decades\,
  he has fronted the band Twice As Good as its lead vocalist and guitarist.
  His 2022 solo debut album earned him the nickname "the world champion\," 
 propelling him on tours across the U.S. and internationally. Paul’s musi
 c fuses Blues\, R&B\, Pop\, and Native American sounds—a heartfelt tribu
 te to his Elem Pomo tribal roots. Inspired by legends like B.B. King\, Rob
 ert Randolph\, Al Green\, and Bruno Mars\, he delivers powerful\, soulful 
 vocals paired with smooth\, melodic guitar lines that keep crowds dancing.
  His artistry has earned him multiple honors\, including the 2010 Native A
 merican Music Award\, 2010 West Coast Blues Hall of Fame Award\, 2013 Indi
 an Summer Music Award\, the 2016 NorBay Music Award\, and the 2023 Yerba B
 uena Center for the Arts Honors.\n\nhttps://paul2xg.com/ https://www.faceb
 ook.com/paul2xg https://www.instagram.com/paul2xg https://www.youtube.com/
 @paul2xg\n\nRecommended If You Like: Tommy Castro\, Stevie Ray Vaughan\, G
 ary Clarke Jr
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 0000EK3OHMA1
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
