BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Winter Magic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T180000
UID:2611166yrLrF6FOkOQYjXUkdsS7w
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  11/15/26\n\nDECEMBER EXHIBIT: WI
 NTER MAGIC\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  November 23– December 27\, 2026\n\nRECEPT
 ION/HOLIDAY OPEN HOUSE: DECEMBER 5\, 2026\, 11am to 6pm: Join in to meet t
 he artists and cheer the season\, the show and enjoy holiday goodies. As p
 art of the festivities\, we will host our monthly free drawing for an artw
 ork by Ron Sumner.  The Gallery is pleased to participate again this year
  in the Healdsburg Chamber’s Holiday Sip & Shop – for more information
 : 2026 Healdsburg Holiday Sip & Shop\, Eventbrite.com.\n\nSonoma County ar
 tists\, Willow LaLand\, Phyllis Rapp\, Linda Loveland Reid\, Laura Roney\,
  Luba Stolper\, Ron Sumner\, Jo Tobin-Charleston\, Carolyn Wilson and Gen 
 Zorich present Winter Magic\, a mix of unique artistic expressions creatin
 g a magical welcome to the 2026 holiday season.  Starting with nature’s
  magic -the colorful painterly skies at dawn and dusk – LaLand’s “Bo
 ston Harbor” at sunrise engenders warm feelings of hope as does Roney’
 s “Dancing in the Snow” in the waning rays of daylight.  Stolper weav
 es a spell with “Whispering Elegance\,” objects so real – the lace\,
  the cherries\, the vase- the viewer is drawn in awe.  Wilson’s “New 
 Beginnings” draws the viewer’s eye with lively colorful flowers that s
 eem to dance for joy.  Artists Rapp and Sumner turn to our feline and fea
 thered friends for inspiration:  in Rapp’s “Emerald Eye\,” the kitt
 y captivates us with a mesmerizing gaze and Sumner’s “Snowy Owl” loo
 ks out from its perch in a moonlit snowy glen.   From our abstract artis
 ts\, Reid lights our spirit with “Green for Joy” and Zorich’s “Lay
 ers and Red Rock\, “compelling in texture with splashes of random color 
 shapes. To enable us to cast one’s own spell\, Tobin-Charleston’s spar
 kle/colored-themed crystal pendant sets are the perfect ticket.\n\nAll mem
 ber artists are showing many smaller works throughout the Gallery\, ideal 
 for gifting.\n\nFor the Holiday Season our Staircase Showcase features man
 y different hand-crafted 3D artist offerings. Ceramic artists Kathy Brown\
 , Joann Cassady\, Ed Price\, Karen Norton and Steve Sanders offer a variet
 y of vases\, platters\, and bowls.  Our glass artists\, Brian & Nancy Rob
 erts\, Melissa McCann and Tim Montesouti present gorgeous fused glass art\
 , decorative boxes\, and tree ornaments. Plus\, we have horsehair bowls an
 d decorated gourds by Susan Miron and wooden bird sculptures presented by 
 Amber Biocca. And\, as always\, there is jewelry throughout the gallery. Y
 ou can find the perfect earrings\, necklace\, pendant or bracelet from our
  local jewelers: Galley-member Jo Tobin-Charleston\, Aaron Poovey\, Laura 
 Buckner\, Melissa McCann\, Patricia Reilly\, Hamida Judith Dides\, Elaine 
 Greene\, Heyoka Merrifield\, and JoAnna Noble.\n\nJOIN US for ARTNITE HEAL
 DSBURG\, THURSDAY\, DECEMBER 3  5:00 – 7:00 pm : Artnite Healdsburg is 
 a community event celebrating art and creativity with more than 20 galleri
 es participating\, along with select restaurants\, bars and boutiques. \n
 \nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707
 \\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm\; extended holiday hours: Open Fr
 i & Sat 10am – 7pm through December 23rd\; closed December 25.    www
 .upstairsartgallery.net \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird
 \, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Winter Magic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T180000
UID:261115vGiVrquNA06IhhDtaEPeFA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  11/15/26\n\n**DECEMBER EXHIBIT: 
 WINTER MAGIC**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  November 23– December 27\, 2026\n\n**
 RECEPTION/HOLIDAY OPEN HOUSE: DECEMBER 5\, 2026\, 11am to 6pm: Join in to 
 meet the artists and cheer the season\, the show and enjoy holiday goodies
 . As part of the festivities\, we will host our monthly free drawing for a
 n artwork by Ron Sumner.  The Gallery is pleased to participate again thi
 s year in the Healdsburg Chamber’s Holiday Sip & Shop – for more infor
 mation: 2026 Healdsburg Holiday Sip & Shop\, Eventbrite.com.**\n\nSonoma C
 ounty artists\, **Willow LaLand\, Phyllis Rapp\, Linda Loveland Reid\, Lau
 ra Roney\, Luba Stolper\, Ron Sumner\, Jo Tobin-Charleston\, Carolyn Wilso
 n and Gen Zorich** present **Winter Magic\,** a mix of unique artistic exp
 ressions creating a magical welcome to the 2026 holiday season.  Starting
  with nature’s magic -the colorful painterly skies at dawn and dusk – 
 LaLand’s “Boston Harbor” at sunrise engenders warm feelings of hope 
 as does Roney’s “Dancing in the Snow” in the waning rays of daylight
 .  Stolper weaves a spell with “Whispering Elegance\,” objects so rea
 l – the lace\, the cherries\, the vase- the viewer is drawn in awe.  Wi
 lson’s “New Beginnings” draws the viewer’s eye with lively colorfu
 l flowers that seem to dance for joy.  Artists Rapp and Sumner turn to ou
 r feline and feathered friends for inspiration:  in Rapp’s “Emerald E
 ye\,” the kitty captivates us with a mesmerizing gaze and Sumner’s “
 Snowy Owl” looks out from its perch in a moonlit snowy glen.   From ou
 r abstract artists\, Reid lights our spirit with “Green for Joy” and Z
 orich’s “Layers and Red Rock\, “compelling in texture with splashes 
 of random color shapes. To enable us to cast one’s own spell\, Tobin-Cha
 rleston’s sparkle/colored-themed crystal pendant sets are the perfect ti
 cket.\n\nAll member artists are showing many smaller works throughout the 
 Gallery\, ideal for gifting.\n\nFor the Holiday Season our **Staircase Sho
 wcase** features many different hand-crafted 3D artist offerings. Ceramic 
 artists Kathy Brown\, Joann Cassady\, Ed Price\, Karen Norton and Steve Sa
 nders offer a variety of vases\, platters\, and bowls.  Our glass artists
 \, Brian & Nancy Roberts\, Melissa McCann and Tim Montesouti present gorge
 ous fused glass art\, decorative boxes\, and tree ornaments. Plus\, we hav
 e horsehair bowls and decorated gourds by Susan Miron and wooden bird scul
 ptures presented by Amber Biocca. And\, as always\, there is jewelry throu
 ghout the gallery. You can find the perfect earrings\, necklace\, pendant 
 or bracelet from our local jewelers: Galley-member Jo Tobin-Charleston\, A
 aron Poovey\, Laura Buckner\, Melissa McCann\, Patricia Reilly\, Hamida Ju
 dith Dides\, Elaine Greene\, Heyoka Merrifield\, and JoAnna Noble.\n\n**JO
 IN US for ARTNITE HEALDSBURG\, THURSDAY\, DECEMBER 3  5:00 – 7:00 pm** 
 : Artnite Healdsburg is a community event celebrating art and creativity w
 ith more than 20 galleries participating\, along with select restaurants\,
  bars and boutiques. \n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Heald
 sburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm\; extended ho
 liday hours: Open Fri & Sat 10am – 7pm through December 23rd\; closed De
 cember 25.    **www.upstairsartgallery.net** \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Belly Dancing with Raja - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T120000
UID:261107Bg0XHp7E_U6B5V-mdp6bVg
DESCRIPTION:DATE AND TIME: Tuesdays @ 11:00 AM\n\nUnlock your inner streng
 th and find your flow. Belly dancing with Raja is an innovative fusion cl
 ass that blends the rhythmic artistry of belly dance with the high-energ
 y benefits of aerobics. Designed to be both a cardiovascular challenge an
 d a deep toning session\, this class focuses on the “powerhouse” of th
 e body—your core.\n\nBy layering fluid\, isolative movements over an ath
 letic aerobic base\, you will challenge your muscles in ways traditional g
 ym workouts can’t reach.\n\nWhat to Expect in Belly Dancing Class\n\n•
  Core-Centric Power: Use undulations and shimmies to engage deep abdomina
 l muscles for a tighter\, stronger midsection.\n\n• Functional Stability
 : Improve your balance and posture through controlled\, hip-driven moveme
 nts and low-impact aerobic footwork.\n\n• Total Body Toning: Build lean
  muscle in your legs\, glutes\, and arms while maintaining a constant\, he
 art-pumping pace.\n\n• Mind-Body Connection: Enhance your coordination 
 and body awareness through rhythmic\, expressive choreography.\n\n“Wheth
 er you’re looking to define your waistline or simply want a workout that
  feels like a celebration\, this class offers the perfect balance of sweat
  and grace.”\n\nDifficulty Level: All levels welcome! No prior dance ex
 perience is required—just bring your energy and a willingness to move.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/belly-dancing-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
