BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Penngrove Holiday Lights Parade
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T190000
UID:2611164tVqteMn-U6RUnv2Y7XgCA
DESCRIPTION:WHO: Penngrove Social Firemen present\n\nWHAT: Penngrove Holid
 ay Parade of Lights  - 11th Annual  \n\nWHEN: Sunday\, December 13\,
  2026\, from 6:00 pm – 7:00 pm\n\nWHERE: Downtown Penngrove along Main S
 t.\, (the parade forms at Penngrove Park\, 11800 Main Street)\n\nWHY: Holi
 day cheer with lighted farm vehicles\n\n**Holiday Parade of Lights – Dec
 ember 13\, 2026**\n\n Bundle up and come down to Main Street for the 11th
   annual Penngrove Holiday Parade of Lights on Sunday\, **December 13\,
 ** from 6:00 PM to 7:00 PM. Penngrove Social Firemen sponsor the glammed-u
 p tractor-trailers\, farm vehicles\, and decorated farm tractors covered i
 n lights. \n\n Local merchants will serve soup\, pizza\, hot cider\, and
  street food to keep you warm. The parade stages in Penngrove Park\, 1180
 0 Main St.\, and rolls up Main Street toward Adobe Rd. Watch out for the
  train.\n\n Parade entries must register in advance and gather an hour ea
 rly at Penngrove Park. The entry fee is $20 on Parade night. To join the p
 arade\, download the entry form from https://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.o
 rgand return it by December 10 to Penngrove Market or by email to mrsjjav
 a@hotmail.com . For information\, contact Kim Hanson at 707 318-2191.\n\n
 Roads Close: 5:00 - 7:30 pm \n\nParking 4:30 - 8:00 pm at Penngrove Eleme
 ntary School\, Adobe Rd. & Petaluma Hill Road.\n\nPenngrove Social Firemen
  are a nonprofit 501 c3. The own and maintain the Penngrove Clubhouse and 
 Penngrove Park\, and support community needs.
LOCATION:Downtown Penngrove
URL:https://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Weekend Santa Sightings
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T150000
UID:261116-c3cIIcjgkW6sDOGHND-MA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the holidays and join us at the Village for photos w
 ith Santa happening on weekends from Saturday\, November 28th to Sunday\, 
 December 20th\, 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. daily.\n\nAppointments are highly recomm
 ended\, as we cannot guarantee that we can accommodate all walk-ups throug
 hout the event series. Reserve your 5-minute window now for a $35 fee duri
 ng our initial release (through Friday\, November 13). Beginning Saturday\
 , November 14\, the fee increases to $45. Each family will receive a print
  to take home that day\, as well as a digital copy of their photo followin
 g the appointment. Please note that we do not call or text waitlisted gues
 ts.\\*\n\nMake the most of your Santa visit:\n\nYour photo package include
 s up to five digital photos\, emailed the Monday following your appointmen
 t\, plus a print to take home that day.\n\nEnjoy writing letters to Santa 
 and dropping them off at the official Montgomery Village Santa Mail mailbo
 x\, plus crafts at our holiday craft tables.\n\nSweeten your visit! Stop b
 y Salt & Straw before or after your appointment and enjoy a complimentary 
 kids’ scoop with any ice cream purchase during Weekend Santa Sightings (
 valid each Saturday and Sunday from 11/28/26 to 12/20/26 between 11 a.m. t
 o 3 p.m.).\n\nKeep an eye out for ME SPA’s elves\, spreading holiday che
 er and a little stress relief with special cards to redeem at the spa. Bri
 ng yours in for a Chill Bag\, a holiday survival kit filled with goodies a
 nd coupons to help you keep your cool all season long. For an extra moment
  of relaxation\, enjoy a complimentary chair massage as scheduling allows.
 \n\nRetro Foto will be assisting in making this memory last a lifetime by 
 providing Santa with a vintage ride for all to enjoy! Retro Foto is Sonoma
  County’s boutique photo booth experience. Lola is a fully restored 1970
  Volkswagen bus that loves the camera – whether it’s as a photo booth 
 or a photo backdrop! Lola is all about making memories\, which is why Sant
 a thought this would be the perfect way to drive into the Holiday season!\
 n\nBy attending this event\, guests consent to appear in photo/video recor
 dings that may be used for website photography or other purposes.\n\n\\*A 
 portion of proceeds will benefit Sonoma County Secret Santa Program.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village - Courtyard
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/weekend-santa-sightings/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Night with Janis Joplin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T170000
UID:261115hwcXeEcEs0Kl5pu5MXBaEg
DESCRIPTION:A NIGHT WITH JANIS JOPLIN\, starring Libby Oberlin is our Chri
 stmas gift to you! The entire cast is back on board bringing this hit back
  to life! This show musically explores Janis Joplin’s music and well as 
 her musical influences. \n\nWritten\, created and originally directed by 
 Randy Johnson\n\nDirected by Loryn Hatten\n\nOriginally directed at SAL by
  Carl Jordan \n\nStarring Libby Oberlin as Janis Joplin\n\nFeaturing Aja 
 Gianola\, Jeffrie Givens\, Michelle Louise\, Simone Mosely\, and Skylaer P
 alacois \n\nMichelle Louise will be playing the role of Janis Joplin on S
