DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T190000
UID:260915EigudhkcakCVyyTemQ4ZbQ
DESCRIPTION:Broadway Holiday Returns This December! Our beloved holiday tr
 adition is back - with performances at Jackson Theater in Santa Rosa \\(De
 c 12-13\\) and a highly anticipated return to the Sebastiani Theatre in So
 noma \\(Dec 16-20\\)\, where last year's run sold out! Celebrate the seaso
 n with Broadway stars\, festive favorites\, and heartwarming moments. Plus
 \, Gold ticket holders at Jackson Theater at Sonoma County Day are invited
  to an exclusive pre-show reception\, while Gold ticket holders at Sebasti
 ani Theatre attendees can enjoy a post-show reception at The Zina Lounge a
 t Ledson Hotel. SANTA ROSA - Jackson Theater Saturday\, December 12 at 2:0
 0 p.m. and 7:00 p.m. Sunday\, December 13 at 2:00 p.m. Please read our "Th
 ings to Know" section near the bottom of the page for your Santa Rosa perf
 ormance! SONOMA - Sebastiani Theatre Wednesday\, December 16 at 7:00 p.m. 
 Thursday\, December 17 at 7:00 p.m. Friday\, December 18 at 7:00 p.m. Satu
 rday\, December 19 at 2:00 p.m. and 7:00 p.m. Sunday\, December 20 at 2:00
  p.m. Groups of 10 or more can save! Secure group tickets by filling out o
 urGroup Inquiries Form\, or call the box office at877-424-1414 ext. 2.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/broadway-holiday/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fr. Brendan Williams - Poems/Prayers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T190000
UID:260819ZkYENL6yxkepTRuprAJImg
DESCRIPTION:Father Brendan Williams\, chaplain of Bishop's Ranch outside H
 ealdsburg\, in conversation with Denise Low. The intersections of prayer a
 nd poetry are shared inspirations from religious traditions for both of th
 ese poets. They will talk about biblical and other religious texts as subl
 iminal cultural guides as well as deliberate choices they make in their re
 spective practices. Psalms and hymns have long influenced sonnets and toda
 y's short lyrical poems. Ginsberg's Kaddish is an audacious example of int
 ertextual borrowing from Jewish tradition. Williams is a priest\, spiritua
 l director\, yogi\, healer\, scholar\, and teacher of religion. His work s
 pans Western and Eastern esoterica\, indigenous Gaelic lifeways\, meditati
 on\, and contemplative spirituality. He chants old rebel tales\, traces th
 e song-streams of ancient wisdom\, and ferries souls along the mythic rive
 rways of human transformation-guiding people from all walks of life back t
 o their birthright of wholeness and freedom within the great ecology of sp
 irit.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/fr-brendan-williams-poems-prayers/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T170000
UID:261004fasm0RCqjEu1Xa0kEhuFlg
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T170000
UID:260824VM059hOjFEmMecYXteZnRQ
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\n*Maple Magic* *& Winter Wonder* invites
  visitors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativ
 ity\, and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided wal
 ks\, hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by t
 he changing landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the 
 sweet fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experienc
 e the peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
